{
  "title": "At the shop: prices, amounts, and \"there isn't any\"",
  "title_target": "У магазині — U mahazyni",
  "goal": "Ask prices, ask for a certain amount of something, and understand the sentence you'll hear most often in a Ukrainian shop: \"we don't have any\" — along with the ending that always comes with it.",
  "bekal": [
    "ask the price of one item and of several",
    "ask for something with Дайте, будь ласка",
    "understand and use немає + родовий",
    "give amounts with units (кілограм, пляшка, пачка)",
    "ask for the total"
  ],
  "dialogs": [
    {
      "title": "Діалог — Morning at the Bessarabska market",
      "intro": "Ani is shopping at the market. Notice that every time the seller says something **isn't there**, the item's name changes its ending: полуниця becomes полуниці, молоко becomes молока.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Продавець:",
          "text": "[Добрий|DOB-riy] [день|den']! [Що|Shcho] [вам|vam]?",
          "id": "Good afternoon! What can I get you?",
          "literal": "good — day! what — to-you?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Скільки|SKEEL'-ki] [коштує|KOSH-too-yeh] [кілограм|kee-lo-HRAM] [яблук|YAB-look]?",
          "id": "How much is a kilo of apples?",
          "literal": "how-much — costs — kilogram — apples (родовий)?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавець:",
          "text": "[Сорок|SO-rok] [п'ять|pyat'] [гривень|HRI-ven'].",
          "id": "Forty-five hryvnias.",
          "literal": "forty — five — hryvnias (родовий plural)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Дайте|DAI-teh], [будь|bood'] [ласка|LAS-ka], [два|dva] [кілограми|kee-lo-HRA-mi].",
          "id": "Two kilos, please.",
          "literal": "give, be — kindness, two — kilograms."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавець:",
          "text": "[Будь|Bood'] [ласка|LAS-ka]. [Ще|Shcheh] [щось|shchos']?",
          "id": "Here you go. Anything else?",
          "literal": "be — kindness. more — something?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[У|OO] [вас|vas] [є|yeh] [полуниця|po-loo-NI-tsya]?",
          "id": "Do you have strawberries?",
          "literal": "at — you — there-is — strawberry?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавець:",
          "text": "[Полуниці|Po-loo-NI-tsee] [немає|neh-MA-yeh]. [Сезон|Seh-ZON] [закінчився|za-KEEN-chiv-sya].",
          "id": "No strawberries. The season's over.",
          "literal": "strawberry (родовий) — there-isn't. season — has-ended."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Шкода|Shko-DA]. [Тоді|To-DEE] [дайте|DAI-teh] [ще|shcheh] [хліб|khleeb] [і|ee] [молоко|mo-lo-KO].",
          "id": "Too bad. Then I'll also have bread and milk, please.",
          "literal": "pity. then — give — more — bread — and — milk."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавець:",
          "text": "[Молока|Mo-lo-KA] [теж|tezh] [немає|neh-MA-yeh]. [Тільки|TEEL'-ki] [кефір|keh-FEER].",
          "id": "No milk either. Only kefir.",
          "literal": "milk (родовий) — also — there-isn't. only — kefir."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Добре|DOB-reh], [кефір|keh-FEER]. [Скільки|SKEEL'-ki] [з|z] [мене|MEH-neh]?",
          "id": "OK, kefir then. How much do I owe you?",
          "literal": "good, kefir. how-much — from — me?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Продавець:",
          "text": "[Сто|Sto] [двадцять|DVAD-tsyat'] [гривень|HRI-ven'].",
          "id": "A hundred and twenty hryvnias.",
          "literal": "hundred — twenty — hryvnias."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Ось|Os'], [будь|bood'] [ласка|LAS-ka]. [Дякую|DYA-koo-yoo]!",
          "id": "Here you are. Thank you!",
          "literal": "here, be — kindness. I-thank!"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "**Скільки коштує for one item, скільки коштують for several.** *Скільки коштує хліб?* (one) — *Скільки коштують яблука?* (several). The verb follows the number of items, just like *is* / *are* in English. If in doubt, point at the item and ask **Скільки це коштує?** — always correct.",
        "**Absence always takes the родовий, and this is the sentence you'll hear most in shops.** *Полуниці немає*, *молока немає*, *хліба немає*. Notice the word order: the item first, *немає* after — the opposite of what you might expect.",
        "**Дайте, будь ласка — the polite command.** Commands in Ukrainian aren't rude as long as *будь ласка* comes with them. To a friend: **дай**. To anyone else, or more than one person: **дайте**. This is the formula you'll use in shops, pharmacies, and kiosks.",
        "**Units change form with the number, like рік in Unit 7.** *Один кілограм*, *два кілограми*, *п'ять кілограмів*. Exactly the same pattern: 1 → dictionary form, 2–4 → ordinary plural, 5 and up → родовий plural.",
        "**The родовий plural often looks like a word with its ending chopped off.** *Яблука* → *яблук*, *гривні* → *гривень*, *книги* → *книг*, *хвилини* → *хвилин*. Feminine nouns in **-а** lose their ending entirely. It feels strange at first, then becomes an easy giveaway.",
        "**Скільки з мене? literally \"how much from me?\"** It's the most common way to ask for the total. Other forms that are just as correct: *Скільки всього?* (how much altogether) or *Скільки за все?*",
        "**Ось = here you are.** Used when handing something over, like English \"here\". To point at something farther away: **он** (*он там* — over there)."
      ],
